0..76 Comment "// A returner\'s row may stay open through a row variable, an implicit of the"
77..164 Comment "// kind `Row` (#2270): `log` prints through `std.io.Console.Eff` and leaves the rest of"
165..240 Comment "// its row to its caller, so one definition is used under every row holding"
241..325 Comment "// `std.io.Console.Eff`, the variable solved at each call by the row equation, and a"
326..423 Comment "// handler of `std.io.Console.Eff` takes `[std.io.Console.Eff | r]` to `[r]`, forwarding the rest"
424..498 Comment "// (Hillerström and Lindley, \"Liberating Effects with Rows and Handlers\","
499..578 Comment "// Type-Driven Development 2016, § 2.5 and § 3.3, T-HANDLER). What refuses is"
579..633 Comment "// in `../../pathological/control/row-variable.gandr`."
635..718 Comment "/// A line printed through `std.io.Console.Eff`, the rest of the row left open: `r`"
719..782 Comment "/// lacks `std.io.Console.Eff`, which the row writes beside it."
